- That's right. - I agree with that.

1042
00:37:08,323 --> 00:37:10,933
- Let's say I make seaweed soup. - Okay.

1043
00:37:11,133 --> 00:37:13,192
I add leftover kimchi to the leftover seaweed soup...

1044
00:37:13,193 --> 00:37:14,903
- for another meal. - To the seaweed soup?

1045
00:37:15,103 --> 00:37:16,162
What?

1046
00:37:16,163 --> 00:37:17,302
(What do you add...)

1047
00:37:17,303 --> 00:37:18,572
(to the seaweed soup?)

1048
00:37:18,573 --> 00:37:21,742
I eat the seaweed and kimchi soup for another meal...

1049
00:37:21,743 --> 00:37:23,812
- and have some leftovers. - Okay.

1050
00:37:23,813 --> 00:37:25,073
Then I stir-fry rice with it.

1051
00:37:25,513 --> 00:37:27,443
- Not even dogs will eat that. - My goodness.

1052
00:37:27,543 --> 00:37:29,282
- Hey, not even dogs will eat that. - Listen.

1053
00:37:29,283 --> 00:37:32,082
- Is it tasty? - Unless I stop eating it,

1054
00:37:32,083 --> 00:37:34,083
it'll go on forever.

1055
00:37:34,253 --> 00:37:35,652
You'll use it like the perpetual broth.

1056
00:37:35,653 --> 00:37:36,882
- It'll keep getting a new life. - The perpetual broth!

1057
00:37:36,883 --> 00:37:37,953
It'll go on.

1058
00:37:38,993 --> 00:37:40,393
No other chefs can copy him.

1059
00:37:43,323 --> 00:37:44,933
(Emptying)

1060
00:37:45,093 --> 00:37:48,333
(He soaks seaweed, the key ingredient.)

1061
00:37:50,303 --> 00:37:52,003
He cooks with ease.

1062
00:37:52,633 --> 00:37:54,303
Did you add olive oil?

1063
00:37:54,673 --> 00:37:57,742
I was going to add sesame oil.

1064
00:37:57,743 --> 00:37:58,772
You bought sesame oil earlier.

1065
00:37:58,773 --> 00:38:00,273
- Didn't you have it? - I forgot.

1066
00:38:00,543 --> 00:38:02,483
- Olive oil is healthy. - That's right.

1067
00:38:03,643 --> 00:38:07,283
(He adds meat to the healthy olive oil.)

1068
00:38:07,383 --> 00:38:09,423
- Is that duck? - It's pork.

1069
00:38:09,583 --> 00:38:12,693
What? Who adds pork to seaweed soup?

1070
00:38:12,853 --> 00:38:13,993
Not beef?

1071
00:38:14,963 --> 00:38:17,392
- I think outside the box. - Right.

1072
00:38:17,393 --> 00:38:18,792
(He seeks freedom by thinking outside the box.)

1073
00:38:18,793 --> 00:38:20,393
He thinks outside the box when he cooks.

1074
00:38:21,033 --> 00:38:24,273
(He flaunts his cooking philosophy.)

1075
00:38:25,273 --> 00:38:28,073
That's right. It should've been sesame oil.

1076
00:38:28,373 --> 00:38:30,073
I added olive oil by mistake.

1077
00:38:31,343 --> 00:38:35,043
(Although it's belated, he adds some sesame oil.)

1078
00:38:37,153 --> 00:38:40,523
(He stir-fries meat diligently.)

1079
00:38:41,023 --> 00:38:43,583
(Serious)

1080
00:38:44,793 --> 00:38:46,322
(He hasn't shown such refreshing skills...)

1081
00:38:46,323 --> 00:38:49,462
(since making his perpetual fried rice.)

1082
00:38:49,463 --> 00:38:50,743
It's like "Culinary Class Wars."

1083
00:38:51,893 --> 00:38:53,433
I don't know if I told you this.

1084
00:38:54,133 --> 00:38:56,362
My dad wanted to send me off...

1085
00:38:56,363 --> 00:38:58,633
to a culinary high school.

1086
00:38:58,973 --> 00:39:01,242
It was his plan to open a restaurant for me...

1087
00:39:01,243 --> 00:39:02,342
after retiring as a civil servant.

1088
00:39:02,343 --> 00:39:05,573
That was his thought behind his desire to send me there.

1089
00:39:05,813 --> 00:39:08,213
Who knows what would've happened had I attended that school?

1090
00:39:08,383 --> 00:39:10,143
I might've starred in "Culinary Class Wars."

1091
00:39:10,883 --> 00:39:11,953
No.

1092
00:39:12,953 --> 00:39:14,322
(However, he became a dark cook.)

1093
00:39:14,323 --> 00:39:15,782
A dark cook?

1094
00:39:15,783 --> 00:39:17,693
(However, he became a dark cook.)

1095
00:39:18,323 --> 00:39:21,922
(He's a cooking monster who stir-fries all ingredients.)

1096
00:39:21,923 --> 00:39:24,063
I think it's the same as drawing.

1097
00:39:24,463 --> 00:39:26,063
It's the act of creating new things.

1098
00:39:26,763 --> 00:39:29,133
His nickname is Stir-Fry Monster.

1099
00:39:30,573 --> 00:39:31,672
(He adds oysters that are in season to the pot.)

1100
00:39:31,673 --> 00:39:34,942
- I planned to use Manila clams. - Right.

1101
00:39:34,943 --> 00:39:36,542
- But they weren't in season. - No.

1102
00:39:36,543 --> 00:39:37,673
So I used oysters instead.

1103
00:39:38,213 --> 00:39:40,443
(He adds garlic as well.)

1104
00:39:41,213 --> 00:39:43,483
(Stir-frying)

1105
00:39:46,883 --> 00:39:49,383
(He adds soaked seaweed as well.)

1106
00:39:50,053 --> 00:39:53,723
(Without checking the doneness, he adds water and boils.)

1107
00:39:54,863 --> 00:39:56,792
I don't like to follow the rules.

1108
00:39:56,793 --> 00:39:59,113
- That's right. It isn't fun. - I don't like instructions.

1109
00:39:59,663 --> 00:40:02,033
I don't like getting bound by a specific style of art.

1110
00:40:03,103 --> 00:40:04,833
It isn't that hard.

1111
00:40:05,233 --> 00:40:07,873
When I cook, I always know that it'll be tasty.

1112
00:40:08,043 --> 00:40:10,143
Also, I usually don't taste the dish I'm cooking.

1113
00:40:10,303 --> 00:40:12,673
But I tasted the dish today too.

1114
00:40:13,313 --> 00:40:14,682
My goodness.

1115
00:40:14,683 --> 00:40:15,742
(The confident Stir-Fry Monster tasted the dish...)

1116
00:40:15,743 --> 00:40:16,782
(for Yoon Kyung Mi, the judge.)

1117
00:40:16,783 --> 00:40:18,083
It's in my hand.

1118
00:40:18,313 --> 00:40:20,053
Is she a judge?

1119
00:40:22,383 --> 00:40:24,822
(For the veteran judge, he controls the saltiness carefully.)

1120
00:40:24,823 --> 00:40:26,923
(Tasting)

1121
00:40:27,363 --> 00:40:28,463
It's nice.

1122
00:40:30,123 --> 00:40:31,293
The name of the dish is...

1123
00:40:33,063 --> 00:40:34,963
Pig That Married Oyster.

1124
00:40:37,033 --> 00:40:39,133
Pig That Married Oyster.

1125
00:40:39,333 --> 00:40:41,453
- I came up with the name. - Pig That Married Oyster.

1126
00:40:41,573 --> 00:40:43,742
Let me tell you what the name reminds you of.

1127
00:40:43,743 --> 00:40:45,913
When you go to your grandparents' place,

1128
00:40:46,373 --> 00:40:47,782
some restaurants have an ambitious name...

1129
00:40:47,783 --> 00:40:49,143
on a faded signboard.

1130
00:40:50,683 --> 00:40:52,243
- You know what I mean, right? - But...

1131
00:40:52,413 --> 00:40:53,753
- The closed restaurants. - Yes.

1132
00:40:54,223 --> 00:40:56,182
- It's a cute name. - I'm so curious...

1133
00:40:56,183 --> 00:40:57,393
about the taste.

1134
00:40:57,753 --> 00:41:00,863
This seaweed soup contains oysters...

1135
00:41:01,093 --> 00:41:02,263
and pork.

1136
00:41:03,163 --> 00:41:04,593
I don't think they wanted that.

1137
00:41:05,733 --> 00:41:06,832
It's nice.

1138
00:41:06,833 --> 00:41:08,563
(It's a pretty nice wedding.)

1139
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:10,872
Pig That Married Oyster.

1140
00:41:10,873 --> 00:41:14,073
(Pig That Married Oyster)

1141
00:41:15,303 --> 00:41:16,673
I just need to wait for the rice.

1142
00:41:18,073 --> 00:41:20,473
Shall I take out some kimchi I made this year?

1143
00:41:21,943 --> 00:41:24,612
This is the kimchi I made this year. This is the fresh kimchi.

1144
00:41:24,613 --> 00:41:26,883
- It's really tasty. - Put some there.

1145
00:41:28,683 --> 00:41:30,523
(Opening)

1146
00:41:31,123 --> 00:41:34,623
(She brought kimchi from Jeju Island and filled Kian84's fridge.)

1147
00:41:35,093 --> 00:41:36,792
(Mom's precious kimchi)

1148
00:41:36,793 --> 00:41:37,932
That's all you need.

1149
00:41:37,933 --> 00:41:39,493
(That's all you need for a tasty meal.)

1150
00:41:43,833 --> 00:41:45,033
Gosh, that's..

1151
00:41:45,373 --> 00:41:46,473
Green onion kimchi.

1152
00:41:46,673 --> 00:41:47,773
Gosh, that's..

1153
00:41:49,243 --> 00:41:50,643
I'd make ramyeon right away.

1154
00:41:51,543 --> 00:41:52,572
Let's eat this.

1155
00:41:52,573 --> 00:41:53,573
(Grabbing)

1156
00:41:54,183 --> 00:41:55,283
- Mom. - Yes?

1157
00:41:56,043 --> 00:41:58,512
You must be tired from being on the plane all day.

1158
00:41:58,513 --> 00:41:59,983
(A small present for his tired mom)

1159
00:42:00,583 --> 00:42:01,822
(He gives one to his mom first.)

1160
00:42:01,823 --> 00:42:02,983
Well done.

1161
00:42:11,063 --> 00:42:12,193
It's tasty.

1162
00:42:12,893 --> 00:42:14,832
I need to take it to restore my stamina.

1163
00:42:14,833 --> 00:42:16,779
(After using a short break to restore his stamina, )

1164
00:42:16,803 --> 00:42:20,032
(he moves Pig That Married Oyster to the table.)

1165
00:42:20,033 --> 00:42:21,303
I'll put it here.

1166
00:42:23,873 --> 00:42:27,913
(He forgoes a trivet for the presentation.)

1167
00:42:28,013 --> 00:42:30,183
- We might not have enough rice. - What?

1168
00:42:30,313 --> 00:42:31,959
- We might not have enough rice. - That's a lot.

1169
00:42:31,983 --> 00:42:33,853
Didn't you burn the rice?

1170
00:42:34,083 --> 00:42:35,782
The bottom was a bit burnt,

1171
00:42:35,783 --> 00:42:37,523
- but it was fine otherwise. - You're good.

1172
00:42:38,123 --> 00:42:41,123
I was worried, but you did much better than I expected.

1173
00:42:42,093 --> 00:42:43,623
(Opening)

1174
00:42:45,363 --> 00:42:47,193
(He transfers meat to the pan using hands.)

1175
00:42:47,833 --> 00:42:51,102
She said she wouldn't eat meat, but I felt like I should cook some.

1176
00:42:51,103 --> 00:42:53,133
That's right. You need your protein.

1177
00:42:53,903 --> 00:42:57,712
(Stir-Fry Monster pan-fries meat with his burning filial love.)

1178
00:42:57,713 --> 00:43:00,013
You really look like a chef.

1179
00:43:01,943 --> 00:43:04,482
Moms don't eat meat unless their sons ask for it.

1180
00:43:04,483 --> 00:43:06,882
That's right. I pan-fried meat on purpose.

1181
00:43:06,883 --> 00:43:07,953
Well done.

1182
00:43:10,323 --> 00:43:11,423
Take a seat.

1183
00:43:12,293 --> 00:43:14,323
Gosh, there are many side dishes.

1184
00:43:15,063 --> 00:43:16,092
Oh, my.

1185
00:43:16,093 --> 00:43:19,493
(With love, Stir-Fry Monster made a birthday meal for his mom.)

1186
00:43:20,633 --> 00:43:23,303
(Meat has been pan-fried nicely.)

1187
00:43:24,233 --> 00:43:26,633
(Rice cooked in a pot is fluffy.)

1188
00:43:26,933 --> 00:43:29,843
(There's Mom's kimchi from Jeju Island.)

1189
00:43:31,113 --> 00:43:34,843
(Then there's me, Pig That Married Oyster!)

1190
00:43:36,343 --> 00:43:38,343
It's like the wedding between an oyster and a pig.

1191
00:43:38,983 --> 00:43:41,253
Let's eat. Oh, my.

1192
00:43:42,053 --> 00:43:44,193
- Happy birthday, Mom. - Thank you.

1193
00:43:44,823 --> 00:43:46,993
(Enjoy the food.)

1194
00:43:47,363 --> 00:43:48,593
Try the kimchi.

1195
00:43:48,863 --> 00:43:50,162
- Did you make it? - Yes.

1196
00:43:50,163 --> 00:43:52,243
(She finally tastes Stir-Fry Monster's masterpiece.)

1197
00:43:52,563 --> 00:43:53,992
I'm curious to see how she will react to it.

1198
00:43:53,993 --> 00:43:55,003
(How is it?)

1199
00:43:56,261 --> 00:43:57,760
I'm curious to see how she will react to it.

1200
00:43:57,761 --> 00:43:59,121
(How does the seaweed soup taste?)

1201
00:43:59,931 --> 00:44:01,661
You did well to make the seaweed soup.

1202
00:44:01,731 --> 00:44:03,001
- Is it okay? - Really?

1203
00:44:03,361 --> 00:44:04,501
Was she really hungry?

1204
00:44:05,101 --> 00:44:07,181
(The Stir-Fry Monster quickly tries a bite as well.)

1205
00:44:07,231 --> 00:44:08,301
What?

1206
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:10,701
- It's good. - Right. It's good.

1207
00:44:11,441 --> 00:44:12,611
You did well.

1208
00:44:14,011 --> 00:44:15,740
Oysters and pork must go well together.

1209
00:44:15,741 --> 00:44:17,857
- They worked well together. - Wasn't the oyster fishy?

1210
00:44:17,881 --> 00:44:19,910
The oyster's refreshing...

1211
00:44:19,911 --> 00:44:22,451
and strong taste...

1212
00:44:22,651 --> 00:44:25,191
was balanced with the pork's clean taste.

1213
00:44:26,191 --> 00:44:27,821
So they both ate each other.

1214
00:44:28,191 --> 00:44:29,961
- The two were meant to be. - Right.

1215
00:44:30,391 --> 00:44:32,091
- I cook well. - Right.

1216
00:44:32,661 --> 00:44:35,061
(The birthday meal he made for his mother is a success.)

1217
00:44:36,761 --> 00:44:39,770
(It's been a while for them to have a nice meal together.)

1218
00:44:39,771 --> 00:44:41,141
The seaweed soup is good.

1219
00:44:41,771 --> 00:44:42,771
(She enjoys her son's seaweed soup.)

1220
00:44:42,772 --> 00:44:44,570
She's really enjoying it.

1221
00:44:44,571 --> 00:44:45,571
It must be good.

1222
00:44:45,572 --> 00:44:47,111
It was her first meal that day.

1223
00:44:47,841 --> 00:44:50,041
It tastes even better because my son made it.

1224
00:44:50,481 --> 00:44:53,380
The seaweed soup would taste good with the green onion kimchi.

1225
00:44:53,381 --> 00:44:54,551
Gosh, it's the best.

1226
00:44:55,321 --> 00:44:57,450
Add some water when you heat it up again.

1227
00:44:57,451 --> 00:44:58,521
- Right. - Right.

1228
00:44:58,621 --> 00:44:59,621
It will become salty.

1229
00:45:01,191 --> 00:45:03,261
- It's a bit salty. - Right.

1230
00:45:03,391 --> 00:45:05,561
- What? - It's salty.

1231
00:45:05,731 --> 00:45:07,960
I didn't know if it was salty when it was hot.

1232
00:45:07,961 --> 00:45:10,800
I could taste it accurately once it cooled down.

1233
00:45:10,801 --> 00:45:12,500
That is why I eat food quickly.

1234
00:45:12,501 --> 00:45:13,501
- I see. - I see.

1235
00:45:13,631 --> 00:45:15,771
(So that was why you ate quickly.)

1236
00:45:16,141 --> 00:45:17,401
It's very salty.

1237
00:45:17,571 --> 00:45:19,811
- Just add some water. - I should add some water.

1238
00:45:19,941 --> 00:45:20,941
Right.

1239
00:45:21,341 --> 00:45:23,741
She's eating it as she's happy that her son made it for her.

1240
00:45:24,351 --> 00:45:26,311
This is beef, right? This isn't pork, right?

1241
00:45:26,611 --> 00:45:27,821
It's pork!

1242
00:45:28,351 --> 00:45:29,421
It's pork.

1243
00:45:30,921 --> 00:45:32,721
- Oh, this is pork? - Yes.

1244
00:45:34,691 --> 00:45:35,821
(Humming)

1245
00:45:35,961 --> 00:45:38,561
But how does it taste like this with pork?

1246
00:45:38,631 --> 00:45:40,731
Oh, I see. You put in oysters.

1247
00:45:42,031 --> 00:45:43,601
- It has everything healthy. - Right.

1248
00:45:43,831 --> 00:45:45,731
Everyone needs to think outside the box.

1249
00:45:46,901 --> 00:45:49,101
(The dish of the Dark Spoon who thought out of the box)

1250
00:45:49,141 --> 00:45:51,571
(She scrapes the rice and puts it into the seaweed soup.)

1251
00:45:51,871 --> 00:45:53,671
- Is that enough? - This is enough.

1252
00:45:54,581 --> 00:45:57,241
You eat a lot less now.

1253
00:45:58,051 --> 00:45:59,610
It's like that when you get old.

1254
00:45:59,611 --> 00:46:01,550
It's harder to digest food.

1255
00:46:01,551 --> 00:46:03,621
My mom said the same thing.

1256
00:46:03,981 --> 00:46:05,490
Is it hard for you to digest the food?

1257
00:46:05,491 --> 00:46:06,491
(Worried)

1258
00:46:06,591 --> 00:46:08,060
The rice hasn't been fully cooked.

1259
00:46:08,061 --> 00:46:09,591
What? Really?

1260
00:46:09,891 --> 00:46:10,891
It hasn't been fully cooked?

1261
00:46:10,892 --> 00:46:12,490
Can't you tell? It hasn't been fully cooked.

1262
00:46:12,491 --> 00:46:14,430
It tastes fine. What do you mean?

1263
00:46:14,431 --> 00:46:15,500
It hasn't been fully cooked.

1264
00:46:15,501 --> 00:46:17,261
Stir-Fry Monster has been eliminated.

1265
00:46:17,331 --> 00:46:19,100
- It's good. - That's not what I'm talking about.

1266
00:46:19,101 --> 00:46:21,400
How can you tell me it hasn't been fully cooked after finishing it all?

1267
00:46:21,401 --> 00:46:23,441
- Is that sungnyung? - I decided to make sungnyung.

1268
00:46:24,471 --> 00:46:27,341
(Rummaging)

1269
00:46:27,911 --> 00:46:29,981
I wasn't able to prepare an envelope, Mom.

1270
00:46:30,241 --> 00:46:31,311
What?

1271
00:46:31,851 --> 00:46:33,310
This is your birthday gift.

1272
00:46:33,311 --> 00:46:34,381
Gosh!

1273
00:46:35,181 --> 00:46:36,251
Are you a loan shark?

1274
00:46:36,981 --> 00:46:39,390
- Why not get the gold bills? - Right. You could've done that.

1275
00:46:39,391 --> 00:46:41,621
It's a better feeling like that as it's nice and thick.

1276
00:46:42,121 --> 00:46:44,001
Why didn't you divide it to smaller bills then?

1277
00:46:44,461 --> 00:46:45,930
Those bills were my only choice.

1278
00:46:45,931 --> 00:46:48,131
It looks like he emptied up an ATM.

1279
00:46:49,101 --> 00:46:50,630
(Fortunately, he got out the money normally...)

1280
00:46:50,631 --> 00:46:52,171
(from the ATM in the supermarket.)

1281
00:46:52,671 --> 00:46:55,101
(He got out a thick bundle of bills.)

1282
00:46:55,271 --> 00:46:57,040
I know what you're saying.

1283
00:46:57,041 --> 00:46:59,617
- It feels better with more bills. - As it seems like more money.

1284
00:46:59,641 --> 00:47:01,210
Happy birthday.

1285
00:47:01,211 --> 00:47:02,340
(A big birthday gift)

1286
00:47:02,341 --> 00:47:03,540
It was 1,000 dollars.

1287
00:47:03,541 --> 00:47:05,310
You still should've found something to put it into.

1288
00:47:05,311 --> 00:47:07,157
- There's her genuine smile. - You're giving me...

1289
00:47:07,181 --> 00:47:09,581
cash like that.

1290
00:47:09,681 --> 00:47:11,490
- Thank you! - Here you are.

1291
00:47:11,491 --> 00:47:13,150
This is better than the golden bills.

1292
00:47:13,151 --> 00:47:14,191
Right.

1293
00:47:14,721 --> 00:47:16,021
This is a lot of money.

1294
00:47:16,291 --> 00:47:19,091
Giving money like this helps you spend wisely.

1295
00:47:19,191 --> 00:47:21,301
Right. I should spend wisely. It's from my son.

1296
00:47:22,901 --> 00:47:24,430
(After a big money gift...)

1297
00:47:24,431 --> 00:47:25,501
Here.

1298
00:47:26,271 --> 00:47:27,400
The sungnyung must be good.

1299
00:47:27,401 --> 00:47:29,147
(They go for another round with the warm sungnyung.)

1300
00:47:29,171 --> 00:47:30,701
(Slurping)

1301
00:47:31,411 --> 00:47:33,211
- This is great. Try it. - Is it okay?

1302
00:47:33,711 --> 00:47:35,540
- It's really good. - I like regular rice.

1303
00:47:35,541 --> 00:47:37,441
(You can have all of it, Mom.)

1304
00:47:38,151 --> 00:47:39,580
(Eating)

1305
00:47:39,581 --> 00:47:41,651
Have it with the green onion kimchi.

1306
00:47:41,781 --> 00:47:42,851
Gosh, it's so salty.

1307
00:47:43,621 --> 00:47:44,720
Was it that salty?

1308
00:47:44,721 --> 00:47:46,621
It became much saltier after it cooled down.

1309
00:47:46,821 --> 00:47:48,420
- I still finished a bowl. - What?

1310
00:47:48,421 --> 00:47:50,491
I ate it as you made it for me.

1311
00:47:50,621 --> 00:47:52,731
- I ate it when I was hungry. - Right.

1312
00:47:52,931 --> 00:47:55,161
I can taste it accurately now that I'm full.

1313
00:47:56,131 --> 00:47:58,401
It's hard for something to be bad as your first meal.

1314
00:47:58,831 --> 00:48:00,031
He keeps adding water.

1315
00:48:00,201 --> 00:48:01,971
It's a new start of the perpetual broth.

1316
00:48:03,341 --> 00:48:04,570
(His mom rinses out the saltiness with the sungnyung.)

1317
00:48:04,571 --> 00:48:06,241
It must've been really salty for her.

1318
00:48:07,841 --> 00:48:08,911
Gosh.

1319
00:48:10,081 --> 00:48:11,350
(Looking intently)

1320
00:48:11,351 --> 00:48:12,751
What are the dogs doing?

1321
00:48:13,981 --> 00:48:15,280
- Gosh. - How adorable.

1322
00:48:15,281 --> 00:48:17,201
- They're adapting well. - This is what I think.

1323
00:48:17,351 --> 00:48:19,590
It's much better to see them inside the house.

1324
00:48:19,591 --> 00:48:21,061
- Of course. - Much better.

1325
00:48:21,391 --> 00:48:24,020
- Go out for walks often. - It's a must.

1326
00:48:24,021 --> 00:48:25,390
They need to be out often.

1327
00:48:25,391 --> 00:48:26,790
It would be great for you to exercise as well.

1328
00:48:26,791 --> 00:48:28,601
- Right. - Jeju Island will be great.

1329
00:48:29,901 --> 00:48:31,130
Did you put in more water?

1330
00:48:31,131 --> 00:48:32,847
- That will solve things. - I put in a lot.

1331
00:48:32,871 --> 00:48:36,301
Gosh, I was still served with seaweed soup on my birthday.

1332
00:48:37,741 --> 00:48:38,941
It finally tastes right.

1333
00:48:41,441 --> 00:48:43,680
For my next birthday,

1334
00:48:43,681 --> 00:48:47,680
it would be great to eat with my daughter-in-law.

1335
00:48:47,681 --> 00:48:50,181
Gosh! The conversation always ends with marriage.

1336
00:48:50,381 --> 00:48:51,451
Okay.

1337
00:48:52,151 --> 00:48:54,690
- It has begun. - Next year?

1338
00:48:54,691 --> 00:48:57,091
I heard you will have some luck to get married next year.

1339
00:48:57,191 --> 00:48:58,631
- That was what I was told. - Right.

1340
00:48:58,831 --> 00:49:00,437
I heard you will have some luck to get married next year.

1341
00:49:00,461 --> 00:49:02,201
I felt so jealous to see Jang Woo.

1342
00:49:02,431 --> 00:49:03,831
- Jang Woo? - Right.

1343
00:49:04,701 --> 00:49:06,871
I'll make sure to get married before you turn 70.

1344
00:49:07,371 --> 00:49:09,671
I think my mother's heart has become a lot warmer.

1345
00:49:10,071 --> 00:49:13,371
It felt great to bring over the dogs that were ownerless.

1346
00:49:13,911 --> 00:49:17,581
What's greater for me is that my mother felt really happy.

1347
00:49:18,011 --> 00:49:19,551
That was what brought me joy.

1348
00:49:20,181 --> 00:49:21,621
Alkong and Dalkong.

1349
00:49:22,181 --> 00:49:24,280
I think you two have found a great owner.

1350
00:49:24,281 --> 00:49:27,191
Let's have a great life together.

1351
00:49:28,021 --> 00:49:29,021
Mom!

1352
00:49:29,991 --> 00:49:31,291
Continue to be who you are.

1353
00:49:31,561 --> 00:49:32,631
Nice.

1354
00:49:33,391 --> 00:49:35,930
My son made me seaweed soup.

1355
00:49:35,931 --> 00:49:37,900
You left all of the soup as it was salty.

1356
00:49:37,901 --> 00:49:39,700
No. I had a lot of it.

1357
00:49:39,701 --> 00:49:40,801
The seawater.

1358
00:49:41,441 --> 00:49:42,700
- I can have more. - No!

1359
00:49:42,701 --> 00:49:43,801
Don't force yourself!

1360
00:49:43,971 --> 00:49:45,241
It's still the same.

1361
00:49:46,411 --> 00:49:47,541
It was salty earlier.

1362
00:49:48,781 --> 00:49:50,340
- It was good though. - Right.

1363
00:49:50,341 --> 00:49:52,210
(Let's Be Happy with Alkong and Dalkong)

1364
00:49:52,211 --> 00:49:53,211
(I Live Alone)

1365
00:49:53,381 --> 00:49:56,221
I've waited for this day.

1366
00:49:56,921 --> 00:49:58,321
Well,

1367
00:49:58,891 --> 00:50:00,390
I've really been waiting for this moment.

1368
00:50:00,391 --> 00:50:02,320
- I wondered when you would come. - Oh, thank you.

1369
00:50:02,321 --> 00:50:04,291
I made my hot debut as an officiant,

1370
00:50:04,461 --> 00:50:06,860
and the one who scoffed at me the most is here.

1371
00:50:06,861 --> 00:50:09,231
I watched that episode and you said a lot of things.

1372
00:50:09,461 --> 00:50:11,000
- Oh, right. I'm sorry. - Everything was revealed.

1373
00:50:11,001 --> 00:50:12,031
I couldn't help myself.

1374
00:50:12,601 --> 00:50:14,147
(Hyun Moo was the officiant at Jang Woo's wedding.)

1375
00:50:14,171 --> 00:50:15,941
(My, as for me, I...)

1376
00:50:16,141 --> 00:50:18,311
(He's talking about himself so much.)

1377
00:50:18,841 --> 00:50:22,581
(He couldn't stop his mouth out of excitement.)

1378
00:50:23,411 --> 00:50:25,081
(Ju Seung, you little punk!)

1379
00:50:25,411 --> 00:50:27,081
I went ahead of myself.

1380
00:50:27,921 --> 00:50:29,521
Right.

1381
00:50:30,421 --> 00:50:31,720
"Adrenaline."

1382
00:50:31,721 --> 00:50:33,091
It's Christmas!

1383
00:50:35,121 --> 00:50:36,191
Gosh, it's cold!

1384
00:50:36,921 --> 00:50:37,960
Gosh, it's cold!

1385
00:50:37,961 --> 00:50:39,330
(Ju Seung has come out in his martial arts uniform.)

1386
00:50:39,331 --> 00:50:40,491
You're in that uniform again!

1387
00:50:40,961 --> 00:50:42,131
It's really comfortable.

1388
00:50:42,161 --> 00:50:44,971
(He enjoys winter with his favorite uniform.)

1389
00:50:46,631 --> 00:50:49,301
(He starts running somewhere.)

1390
00:50:50,401 --> 00:50:51,471
Hello.

1391
00:50:51,771 --> 00:50:52,971
(Hi!)

1392
00:50:54,041 --> 00:50:55,880
(He keeps moving after saying hello to the elder in town.)

1393
00:50:55,881 --> 00:50:57,781
- He's doing a Fun Run. - Right.

1394
00:50:57,911 --> 00:50:59,111
He's influenced by me.

1395
00:50:59,811 --> 00:51:01,720
He was a slow-jogging member with you.

1396
00:51:01,721 --> 00:51:03,151
Right. I influenced him a lot.

1397
00:51:04,451 --> 00:51:06,491
(Just like his muse, Hyun Moo, )

1398
00:51:07,221 --> 00:51:09,660
(he's doing a slow Fun Run.)

1399
00:51:09,661 --> 00:51:10,721
Gosh, this is great.

1400
00:51:13,461 --> 00:51:16,031
(Ju Seung starts slowing down.)

1401
00:51:16,961 --> 00:51:18,901
A lot of my seniors are here today.

1402
00:51:19,631 --> 00:51:20,870
(The place he has come to early in the morning)

1403
00:51:20,871 --> 00:51:23,270
It's a place I visit often that's very closeby.

1404
00:51:23,271 --> 00:51:26,911
This is the mountain gym in my area.

1405
00:51:27,611 --> 00:51:29,711
The sunlight and my seniors.

1406
00:51:31,111 --> 00:51:33,280
My seniors are exercising there.

1407
00:51:33,281 --> 00:51:35,321
Even though they are fairly old,

1408
00:51:35,481 --> 00:51:38,921
I see them do their best to work out their muscles.

1409
00:51:39,091 --> 00:51:40,951
That helps me freshen up my mind.

1410
00:51:41,261 --> 00:51:44,261
We had the Innocent Moo-Ku Fall Field Day recently.

1411
00:51:44,461 --> 00:51:46,730
I got quite shocked that day.

1412
00:51:46,731 --> 00:51:49,161
I realized that I was out of shape.

1413
00:51:50,331 --> 00:51:52,630
(The sprint during the Innocent Moo-Ku Fall Field Day)

1414
00:51:52,631 --> 00:51:53,800
He was awful.

1415
00:51:53,801 --> 00:51:56,571
It was because you didn't make the face of a monkey.

1416
00:51:57,571 --> 00:51:58,971
Doing that makes you run faster.

1417
00:51:59,141 --> 00:52:00,440
Ji Hyeon was so fast.

1418
00:52:00,441 --> 00:52:02,761
(He finished last as he didn't make the face of a monkey.)

1419
00:52:02,941 --> 00:52:05,351
This was shocking. He lost to Jang Woo.

1420
00:52:06,011 --> 00:52:09,181
(Do you know why Ju Seung can't run well?)

1421
00:52:09,781 --> 00:52:12,321
(I don't know why he runs like a duck.)

1422
00:52:12,951 --> 00:52:14,721
(He was ridiculed in front of everyone.)

1423
00:52:15,061 --> 00:52:17,861
That was why I decided to reset my heart...

1424
00:52:17,991 --> 00:52:20,061
and get back into shape.

1425
00:52:20,161 --> 00:52:22,600
I've been working out outside in the winter.

1426
00:52:22,601 --> 00:52:24,137
(He started working out outside in the winter.)

1427
00:52:24,161 --> 00:52:27,131
(That was why Ju Seung came out early in the morning.)

1428
00:52:29,071 --> 00:52:30,300
(Martial Artist Ju Seung's pride was hurt.)

1429
00:52:30,301 --> 00:52:32,570
- That was a long time ago. - A lot of time has passed.

1430
00:52:32,571 --> 00:52:34,240
- He's good. - That was four years ago.

1431
00:52:34,241 --> 00:52:35,457
(I will try to recover my reputation.)

1432
00:52:35,481 --> 00:52:37,710
To have the same heart, I dressed up in the same outfit.

1433
00:52:37,711 --> 00:52:39,081
- I see. - Right.

1434
00:52:41,081 --> 00:52:44,351
(He starts with a simple warmup.)

1435
00:52:46,991 --> 00:52:48,961
(Okay. Let's go.)

1436
00:52:55,501 --> 00:52:59,531
(He starts crawling on the floor.)

1437
00:53:00,471 --> 00:53:02,871
- That looks tough to do. - That's tough to do.

1438
00:53:03,171 --> 00:53:05,641
- It's a full-body workout. - It's a workout we haven't seen.

1439
00:53:06,211 --> 00:53:07,240
Three.

1440
00:53:07,241 --> 00:53:08,880
(What kind of workout are you doing?)

1441
00:53:08,881 --> 00:53:09,881
Go.

1442
00:53:10,641 --> 00:53:14,050
It's a workout that develops the muscles and flexibility.

1443
00:53:14,051 --> 00:53:15,180
It's the Spider-Man pushup.

1444
00:53:15,181 --> 00:53:17,991
Spider-Man climbs walls.

1445
00:53:18,751 --> 00:53:20,151
This is done on the ground instead.

1446
00:53:20,591 --> 00:53:22,121
Like this and this.

1447
00:53:23,191 --> 00:53:24,520
(Fully focused)

1448
00:53:24,521 --> 00:53:25,960
A lot of people do that abroad.

1449
00:53:25,961 --> 00:53:28,360
It works as a stretch and pushup at the same time.

1450
00:53:28,361 --> 00:53:30,441
(He gets on the floor as if he was climbing a wall.)

1451
00:53:30,931 --> 00:53:34,031
(It's as if his hands stick to the ground.)

1452
00:53:35,001 --> 00:53:37,701
(It looks like he was climbing a wall when turned around.)

1453
00:53:38,171 --> 00:53:39,641
- Gosh. - I'm climbing a wall.

1454
00:53:41,411 --> 00:53:42,711
That's really hard to do.

1455
00:53:43,211 --> 00:53:44,240
Twenty.

1456
00:53:44,241 --> 00:53:45,711
(That's a fascinating young man.)

1457
00:53:48,581 --> 00:53:50,951
(He tidies up his pants next.)

1458
00:53:51,421 --> 00:53:53,791
Let's go!

1459
00:53:54,391 --> 00:53:55,860
- He's cheering himself up. - Who are you saying that to?

1460
00:53:55,861 --> 00:53:57,941
(It's time to wake up now, Martial Artist Ju Seung.)

1461
00:53:58,361 --> 00:54:01,531
(He does a straight handstand.)

1462
00:54:01,801 --> 00:54:02,860
(He even does pushups on top of that.)

1463
00:54:02,861 --> 00:54:04,230
- There you go. - That's surprising.

1464
00:54:04,231 --> 00:54:05,500
- Not everyone can do that. - While doing a handstand?

1465
00:54:05,501 --> 00:54:06,630
That's insane.

1466
00:54:06,631 --> 00:54:08,271
When cold air comes through,

1467
00:54:08,371 --> 00:54:10,440
it makes me realize I'm alive.

1468
00:54:10,441 --> 00:54:12,041
When we take cold showers,

1469
00:54:12,241 --> 00:54:13,910
there's a rush of adrenaline.

1470
00:54:13,911 --> 00:54:15,611
- It's just like that. - My gosh!

1471
00:54:16,111 --> 00:54:18,110
Why do they keep playing videos of wild animals?

1472
00:54:18,111 --> 00:54:19,811
And it's always so sudden.

1473
00:54:20,651 --> 00:54:24,181
One, two, three, four.

1474
00:54:25,221 --> 00:54:26,850
(He easily pulls off the advanced workout.)

1475
00:54:26,851 --> 00:54:28,461
That's really hard to do.

1476
00:54:28,891 --> 00:54:29,891
(Letting out a shout)

1477
00:54:31,691 --> 00:54:34,361
(His face starts getting crumpled up even more.)

1478
00:54:34,561 --> 00:54:36,641
He must've used all his strength with the handstand.

1479
00:54:37,301 --> 00:54:38,301
(Groaning)

1480
00:54:39,331 --> 00:54:40,370
(Flapping)

1481
00:54:40,371 --> 00:54:41,540
What's that?

1482
00:54:41,541 --> 00:54:43,601
(He ends up stopping during his flap.)

1483
00:54:43,941 --> 00:54:45,541
(Should I try this instead?)

1484
00:54:46,511 --> 00:54:48,180
I was inspired by Hyun Moo.

1485
00:54:48,181 --> 00:54:49,881
I must inspire you a lot.

1486
00:54:50,881 --> 00:54:52,250
He copies every single move I do.

1487
00:54:52,251 --> 00:54:54,311
He's a follower of yours.

1488
00:54:55,681 --> 00:54:56,720
Gosh.

1489
00:54:56,721 --> 00:54:57,721
(Panting)

1490
00:54:57,722 --> 00:54:59,290
(He does it until the end even as he cries out.)

1491
00:54:59,291 --> 00:55:00,291
Twenty-three!

1492
00:55:01,121 --> 00:55:02,190
Right.

1493
00:55:02,191 --> 00:55:04,561
(Mumbling)

1494
00:55:05,331 --> 00:55:06,490
(He does his best to recover his reputation as a martial artist.)

1495
00:55:06,491 --> 00:55:08,201
That must've been a big shock to you.

1496
00:55:08,561 --> 00:55:10,401
Twenty-four. Let's do one more.

1497
00:55:10,931 --> 00:55:12,100
- One more. - One more.

1498
00:55:12,101 --> 00:55:13,461
- One more. - He's going to do 25.

1499
00:55:14,471 --> 00:55:15,870
(Screaming)

1500
00:55:15,871 --> 00:55:17,470
Twenty-five.

1501
00:55:17,471 --> 00:55:18,611
(That's enough.)

1502
00:55:18,871 --> 00:55:19,871
(Groaning)

1503
00:55:20,641 --> 00:55:21,641
(Panting)

1504
00:55:23,411 --> 00:55:25,551
(He plops down to the ground.)

1505
00:55:25,781 --> 00:55:28,351
(Feeling dizzy)

1506
00:55:28,981 --> 00:55:31,350
(Only the sound of panting can be heard from him.)

1507
00:55:31,351 --> 00:55:32,521
Gosh.

1508
00:55:33,291 --> 00:55:35,090
As I spent 2025,

1509
00:55:35,091 --> 00:55:36,820
I continued to do 25 of them.

1510
00:55:36,821 --> 00:55:37,821
(Responding)

1511
00:55:37,822 --> 00:55:39,060
If I do 26 next year,

1512
00:55:39,061 --> 00:55:41,361
I'll be increasing the numbers by one each year.

1513
00:55:41,861 --> 00:55:43,560
(Impressed)

1514
00:55:43,561 --> 00:55:45,000
It will feel like an upgrade.

1515
00:55:45,001 --> 00:55:46,730
- He didn't say anything amazing. - That's great.

1516
00:55:46,731 --> 00:55:49,001
- That's great. - I love their response.

1517
00:55:49,201 --> 00:55:51,341
- So... - You'll be doing 26!

1518
00:55:51,671 --> 00:55:53,641
(Bright)

1519
00:55:54,341 --> 00:55:56,381
It looks a lot more refreshing than being in a gym.

1520
00:55:56,581 --> 00:55:57,640
Gosh, that was great.

1521
00:55:57,641 --> 00:55:59,011
(Shall I go back home now?)

1522
00:55:59,551 --> 00:56:01,681
(Ju Seung warms up his legs.)

1523
00:56:02,221 --> 00:56:03,921
- It's been a while. - It's his shukuchi!

1524
00:56:04,151 --> 00:56:06,390
- Shukuchi! - You still do that?

1525
00:56:06,391 --> 00:56:08,091
(He excitedly sets off with his shukuchi.)

1526
00:56:08,321 --> 00:56:10,690
But doing that does make him look fast.

1527
00:56:10,691 --> 00:56:11,691
Right.

1528
00:56:11,891 --> 00:56:12,961
Gosh, that's great!

1529
00:56:15,001 --> 00:56:16,261
He looks excited as well.

1530
00:56:16,501 --> 00:56:18,231
I was even faster with my running shoes.

1531
00:56:19,171 --> 00:56:21,601
(Retching)

1532
00:56:22,541 --> 00:56:23,671
Did I overdo myself?

1533
00:56:26,041 --> 00:56:27,041
(Letting out a sigh)

1534
00:56:27,271 --> 00:56:29,210
(Let's just walk normally.)

1535
00:56:29,211 --> 00:56:31,081
But a little bit of that made me feel warm.

1536
00:56:35,681 --> 00:56:38,550
(Ju Seung returns home.)

1537
00:56:38,551 --> 00:56:40,491
Gosh, it's cold. That was tough.

1538
00:56:45,131 --> 00:56:46,291
Let's see.

1539
00:56:48,231 --> 00:56:50,061
I must eat.

1540
00:56:51,261 --> 00:56:55,171
(He fills the pot with water first.)

1541
00:56:58,341 --> 00:57:01,581
(He starts humming at the thought of eating.)

1542
00:57:02,081 --> 00:57:03,241
Should I use this?

1543
00:57:05,611 --> 00:57:06,681
All right.

1544
00:57:08,781 --> 00:57:11,691
What is that rectangular pan? Did you buy that?

1545
00:57:11,891 --> 00:57:14,750
I received an award at a movie awards ceremony.

1546
00:57:14,751 --> 00:57:15,860
- That was given as a prize. - Right!

1547
00:57:15,861 --> 00:57:17,260
- Gosh! - Ju Seung won an award!

1548
00:57:17,261 --> 00:57:18,891
Where did you get an award?

1549
00:57:19,091 --> 00:57:20,960
