1570
00:58:02,501 --> 00:58:04,941
I just did a workout and it was winter.

1571
00:58:05,111 --> 00:58:07,141
I needed some fat and protein.

1572
00:58:07,411 --> 00:58:09,241
That was why I prepared some pork belly...

1573
00:58:10,081 --> 00:58:11,381
and to help me warm up,

1574
00:58:12,011 --> 00:58:13,751
I got the spicy stir-fried ramyeon.

1575
00:58:14,481 --> 00:58:16,081
I'm planning to have those two together.

1576
00:58:16,321 --> 00:58:17,680
Should I make some gochujang?

1577
00:58:17,681 --> 00:58:20,221
(Should I make some gochujang?)

1578
00:58:21,521 --> 00:58:23,261
(Getting a generous amount)

1579
00:58:25,531 --> 00:58:27,331
When it comes to pork belly,

1580
00:58:27,631 --> 00:58:29,961
there are people who have ssamjang or gochujang with it.

1581
00:58:30,101 --> 00:58:31,561
But I prefer gochujang.

1582
00:58:31,931 --> 00:58:33,070
- Same here! - Same here!

1583
00:58:33,071 --> 00:58:34,630
- Gochujang? - I prefer gochujang as well.

1584
00:58:34,631 --> 00:58:36,311
- Gochujang tastes better for me. - Right.

1585
00:58:36,501 --> 00:58:38,271
Ssamjang tastes a bit weak.

1586
00:58:38,371 --> 00:58:41,010
As for me, I go for 1.5 portions of gochujang,

1587
00:58:41,011 --> 00:58:42,180
(Gochujang 1.5)

1588
00:58:42,181 --> 00:58:43,311
one portion of sesame oil,

1589
00:58:44,711 --> 00:58:46,011
and one portion of sugar.

1590
00:58:47,681 --> 00:58:48,751
- Gosh! - Gosh!

1591
00:58:50,921 --> 00:58:52,550
(Startled)

1592
00:58:52,551 --> 00:58:53,721
Gosh, what do I do?

1593
00:58:56,061 --> 00:58:57,790
- Since it was winter. - Winter?

1594
00:58:57,791 --> 00:58:59,190
I thought you were in a snow fight.

1595
00:58:59,191 --> 00:59:01,731
It was a snow performance.

1596
00:59:03,101 --> 00:59:04,101
All right.

1597
00:59:04,102 --> 00:59:06,631
(The winter food expert starts cooking again.)

1598
00:59:07,571 --> 00:59:09,900
(He gets a strip of pork belly...)

1599
00:59:09,901 --> 00:59:11,711
(and puts it on top of the heated pan.)

1600
00:59:11,871 --> 00:59:13,341
(Focused)

1601
00:59:13,471 --> 00:59:14,841
(One more strip!)

1602
00:59:15,181 --> 00:59:16,681
(One must have three strips.)

1603
00:59:17,181 --> 00:59:19,581
(He even prepares the ramyeon while cooking the pork belly.)

1604
00:59:21,211 --> 00:59:26,291
(He starts humming as things go smoothly.)

1605
00:59:26,751 --> 00:59:28,220
(Sizzling)

1606
00:59:28,221 --> 00:59:29,291
This is it!

1607
00:59:33,631 --> 00:59:35,260
(He even puts in some kimchi.)

1608
00:59:35,261 --> 00:59:36,301
Nice!

1609
00:59:38,371 --> 00:59:40,971
(I'm a stir-fried ramyeon chef today.)

1610
00:59:41,501 --> 00:59:42,970
(He even plates it nicely.)

1611
00:59:42,971 --> 00:59:44,341
Ju Seung cooks well.

1612
00:59:45,841 --> 00:59:50,311
(The meal gets prepared as he hums.)

1613
00:59:53,381 --> 00:59:55,121
(He picks up the cheese powder.)

1614
00:59:55,621 --> 00:59:58,791
(Tapping)

1615
00:59:59,991 --> 01:00:06,131
(Tapping)

1616
01:00:07,061 --> 01:00:09,200
- Since it was winter. - You have it really high up.

1617
01:00:09,201 --> 01:00:10,830
You must really like that.

1618
01:00:10,831 --> 01:00:13,571
I like the feeling of snow.

1619
01:00:14,071 --> 01:00:16,241
(That's enough.)

1620
01:00:17,271 --> 01:00:18,300
Okay.

1621
01:00:18,301 --> 01:00:21,371
(Winter has come to the bowl of stir-fried ramyeon.)

1622
01:00:22,111 --> 01:00:24,581
(Pork belly is always exciting to see.)

1623
01:00:25,081 --> 01:00:26,981
(There's even his secret gochujang.)

1624
01:00:28,421 --> 01:00:31,851
(Ju Seung's feast is ready.)

1625
01:00:33,621 --> 01:00:34,990
I should send a picture to Mom.

1626
01:00:34,991 --> 01:00:38,260
(I must take a picture of this.)

1627
01:00:38,261 --> 01:00:39,730
The flash went off.

1628
01:00:39,731 --> 01:00:41,490
The food looks bad when the flash goes off.

1629
01:00:41,491 --> 01:00:43,091
- It looked like a crime scene. - Right?

1630
01:00:45,431 --> 01:00:47,370
Thank you for the food.

1631
01:00:47,371 --> 01:00:48,541
(Let's start eating.)

1632
01:00:50,241 --> 01:00:52,741
(He puts the stir-fried ramyeon on top of the pork belly...)

1633
01:00:54,671 --> 01:00:57,311
(and makes a big wrap.)

1634
01:01:00,251 --> 01:01:01,251
(Satisfied)

1635
01:01:05,851 --> 01:01:06,851
(Crunchy)

1636
01:01:09,461 --> 01:01:10,561
Gosh, that's spicy.

1637
01:01:10,921 --> 01:01:12,091
It was too spicy.

1638
01:01:12,461 --> 01:01:15,261
It was even spicier with the spicy stir-fried ramyeon.

1639
01:01:15,701 --> 01:01:17,377
(With the spicy stir-fried ramyeon and the spicy chili pepper, )

1640
01:01:17,401 --> 01:01:18,470
Gosh, it's hot.

1641
01:01:18,471 --> 01:01:20,171
(his mouth starts to burn.)

1642
01:01:21,071 --> 01:01:22,441
(Sucking in air)

1643
01:01:23,541 --> 01:01:24,541
(Groaning)

1644
01:01:25,311 --> 01:01:26,640
He looks like he's about to cry.

1645
01:01:26,641 --> 01:01:29,180
He looks like the dog he dressed up.

1646
01:01:29,181 --> 01:01:30,380
(His eyes look just like Coco's.)

1647
01:01:30,381 --> 01:01:32,511
His eyes look just like Coco's.

1648
01:01:33,611 --> 01:01:36,020
(I can't stop having something good even though it's spicy.)

1649
01:01:36,021 --> 01:01:38,302
You seem to eat food as if it was some kind of challenge.

1650
01:01:39,821 --> 01:01:41,891
(He goes head-to-head with the spicy food.)

1651
01:01:42,161 --> 01:01:43,601
He's going to the restroom for sure.

1652
01:01:45,461 --> 01:01:47,061
(Emptying the plate clean)

1653
01:01:48,191 --> 01:01:49,331
He ate everything.

1654
01:01:50,631 --> 01:01:51,731
Gosh, it's making me drool.

1655
01:01:52,301 --> 01:01:53,371
Gosh, that was good.

1656
01:01:53,501 --> 01:01:55,001
(Clapping)

1657
01:01:55,901 --> 01:01:58,221
I feel too lazy to wash the dishes. Shall I do them later?

1658
01:01:59,011 --> 01:02:01,311
(He pushes back doing the dishes to another time.)

1659
01:02:02,111 --> 01:02:03,380
It's going to be cold.

1660
01:02:03,381 --> 01:02:05,011
(Let's head out.)

1661
01:02:08,921 --> 01:02:11,451
(He heads somewhere while humming winter songs.)

1662
01:02:13,821 --> 01:02:15,790
(The place he heads to excitedly...)

1663
01:02:15,791 --> 01:02:17,391
(is near Yangjae?)

1664
01:02:18,061 --> 01:02:19,691
I'm here.

1665
01:02:22,331 --> 01:02:25,101
(Ju Seung arrives somewhere.)

1666
01:02:25,931 --> 01:02:27,000
All right.

1667
01:02:27,001 --> 01:02:28,400
(Heave-ho!)

1668
01:02:28,401 --> 01:02:29,640
All right.

1669
01:02:29,641 --> 01:02:32,111
(Both of his hands are full with his bags.)

1670
01:02:35,111 --> 01:02:37,511
- He has a bag and a big backpack. - Did he pack a lunchbox?

1671
01:02:38,111 --> 01:02:39,281
Hello.

1672
01:02:41,001 --> 01:02:42,141
Where is this?

1673
01:02:42,671 --> 01:02:43,900
(A place where colorful boxes welcome you)

1674
01:02:43,901 --> 01:02:45,171
It's a toy store!

1675
01:02:45,541 --> 01:02:48,511
I've been coming here often for my hobby.

1676
01:02:48,941 --> 01:02:50,281
It's a model car store.

1677
01:02:51,581 --> 01:02:52,680
I see RC cars too.

1678
01:02:52,681 --> 01:02:54,981
My gosh. I really wanted to buy toy cars from that brand.

1679
01:02:57,051 --> 01:02:59,290
- There are almost every car model. - Exactly.

1680
01:02:59,291 --> 01:03:01,190
At the store, you can also buy products...

1681
01:03:01,191 --> 01:03:03,091
to tune and paint the model cars.

1682
01:03:03,191 --> 01:03:05,331
Here's how I ended up getting into model cars.

1683
01:03:05,731 --> 01:03:09,261
The development of AI has been progressing rapidly lately.

1684
01:03:09,401 --> 01:03:11,631
Our world is going digital quickly.

1685
01:03:11,931 --> 01:03:14,001
So I wanted to go the other way...

1686
01:03:14,171 --> 01:03:16,271
and looked for old-school hobbies.

1687
01:03:17,371 --> 01:03:18,917
That explains my interest in dinosaurs.

1688
01:03:18,941 --> 01:03:21,681
- I want to go back to the old days. - The old days.

1689
01:03:21,941 --> 01:03:23,410
I know what you mean by this.

1690
01:03:23,411 --> 01:03:25,511
I've been getting into watches these days.

1691
01:03:25,851 --> 01:03:28,251
I'm not talking about the automatic ones.

1692
01:03:28,721 --> 01:03:30,180
- I'm into mechanical ones... - Okay.

1693
01:03:30,181 --> 01:03:31,821
- because they're not run by AI. - I see.

1694
01:03:32,321 --> 01:03:33,620
To get that repaired,

1695
01:03:33,621 --> 01:03:35,560
watchmakers would have to work on it...

1696
01:03:35,561 --> 01:03:37,591
for over six months like the old days.

1697
01:03:38,161 --> 01:03:39,161
I really like that.

1698
01:03:39,162 --> 01:03:42,361
Technology has crept far into our daily lives.

1699
01:03:43,701 --> 01:03:44,830
- I just... - You have many machines at home.

1700
01:03:44,831 --> 01:03:46,631
- You have so many of them at home. - Listen.

1701
01:03:47,571 --> 01:03:50,141
(Moomoo's house is filled with machines.)

1702
01:03:50,401 --> 01:03:52,417
I'm into the human touch and old-school hobbies too.

1703
01:03:52,441 --> 01:03:53,571
I didn't know you were too.

1704
01:03:54,371 --> 01:03:55,580
Didn't you interrupt him,

1705
01:03:55,581 --> 01:03:56,810
- so you could steal this idea? - Right.

1706
01:03:56,811 --> 01:03:57,910
(That's right.)

1707
01:03:57,911 --> 01:03:59,211
I'm setting it up.

1708
01:03:59,411 --> 01:04:00,550
- "Old-school hobbies are mine." - Yes.

1709
01:04:00,551 --> 01:04:01,851
Old-School Moo.

1710
01:04:03,421 --> 01:04:04,481
Old-School Moo?

1711
01:04:05,651 --> 01:04:06,921
So I thought of model cars.

1712
01:04:07,521 --> 01:04:09,521
I've been hooked on this hobby for two months now.

1713
01:04:10,321 --> 01:04:12,660
Model cars were first manufactured...

1714
01:04:12,661 --> 01:04:15,031
a long time ago around 1968.

1715
01:04:15,361 --> 01:04:17,041
Some cartoons like "Dash! Yonkuro" were...

1716
01:04:17,201 --> 01:04:18,930
popular in Korea.

1717
01:04:18,931 --> 01:04:20,730
And especially "Bakuso Kyodai Lets and Go" was...

1718
01:04:20,731 --> 01:04:22,570
a huge hit in Korea.

1719
01:04:22,571 --> 01:04:24,141
I really liked this cartoon.

1720
01:04:24,571 --> 01:04:26,471
- It was a huge hit. - I liked this one.

1721
01:04:28,141 --> 01:04:30,010
Guys around my age or slightly older guys...

1722
01:04:30,011 --> 01:04:31,180
probably played with model cars.

1723
01:04:31,181 --> 01:04:32,741
There can't be a single one who didn't.

1724
01:04:32,781 --> 01:04:36,151
Everyone bought model cars...

1725
01:04:36,351 --> 01:04:39,491
and played with them at school back in the day.

1726
01:04:40,251 --> 01:04:41,591
(Dad?)

1727
01:04:42,391 --> 01:04:43,590
It's Choi Min Sik.

1728
01:04:43,591 --> 01:04:44,921
(I'm playing with the toy car.)

1729
01:04:45,731 --> 01:04:47,537
(Back then, in front of the stationery stores...)

1730
01:04:47,561 --> 01:04:49,360
- Right. There were tracks. - I remember that.

1731
01:04:49,361 --> 01:04:50,830
The stores with 360° tracks...

1732
01:04:50,831 --> 01:04:52,471
- were popular. - The 360° tracks. Right.

1733
01:04:52,701 --> 01:04:54,601
- I can smell the childhood vibe... - Right?

1734
01:04:54,771 --> 01:04:56,000
- from the video. - People miss that,

1735
01:04:56,001 --> 01:04:57,177
so they go back to model cars.

1736
01:04:57,201 --> 01:04:59,111
That's right. Oh, how I miss the good old days.

1737
01:04:59,871 --> 01:05:01,511
In the end, this world is a cycle.

1738
01:05:01,841 --> 01:05:03,761
People will come back to the old-school hobbies.

1739
01:05:05,041 --> 01:05:06,911
(The old-school guy's journey of hobbies)

1740
01:05:08,451 --> 01:05:10,651
And nunchucks are retro too.

1741
01:05:11,021 --> 01:05:12,651
- Right. - You like anything retro.

1742
01:05:13,221 --> 01:05:15,021
You can see me here and there on his journey.

1743
01:05:15,091 --> 01:05:16,160
It's the head.

1744
01:05:16,161 --> 01:05:18,081
(He studied dinosaurs to go back to the origin.)

1745
01:05:18,861 --> 01:05:20,260
(He now has a model car hobby, the ideal hobby of the old days.)

1746
01:05:20,261 --> 01:05:22,301
So we've been following the life of one man, right?

1747
01:05:22,861 --> 01:05:24,730
So we've been following the life of one man, right?

1748
01:05:24,731 --> 01:05:26,171
(Laughing)

1749
01:05:26,231 --> 01:05:27,830
What's consistent with your hobbies is that...

1750
01:05:27,831 --> 01:05:29,401
- your hobbies are classic. - Right.

1751
01:05:29,541 --> 01:05:30,861
He's consistent with his hobbies.

1752
01:05:31,871 --> 01:05:32,940
Wait.

1753
01:05:32,941 --> 01:05:34,371
(Whizzing)

1754
01:05:34,641 --> 01:05:36,410
- Hello. - Hello.

1755
01:05:36,411 --> 01:05:37,511
Sir.

1756
01:05:38,011 --> 01:05:39,911
- Wait, the lap time. - You're already here.

1757
01:05:41,511 --> 01:05:42,620
(A model car is racing super fast along the track.)

1758
01:05:42,621 --> 01:05:44,551
- That's super fast. - That's crazy.

1759
01:05:44,821 --> 01:05:46,120
Gosh, it's so fast.

1760
01:05:46,121 --> 01:05:47,221
I broke the record again.

1761
01:05:48,021 --> 01:05:49,421
What? My gosh.

1762
01:05:50,091 --> 01:05:51,190
It's 18.4 seconds.

1763
01:05:51,191 --> 01:05:53,361
- My gosh. What? Eighteen seconds? - This...

1764
01:05:53,761 --> 01:05:55,061
It's 18.49 seconds.

1765
01:05:55,631 --> 01:05:58,300
Actually, anyone with a hint of interest in model cars knows him.

1766
01:05:58,301 --> 01:05:59,331
- Really? - Really?

1767
01:05:59,701 --> 01:06:01,841
He's also a model car painter.

1768
01:06:03,541 --> 01:06:05,210
- He's such a good painter. - Gosh.

1769
01:06:05,211 --> 01:06:07,411
His skills are on another level.

1770
01:06:07,671 --> 01:06:11,241
I also wanted to paint my own model car.

1771
01:06:11,711 --> 01:06:13,281
So I could have a car of my own.

1772
01:06:13,381 --> 01:06:14,861
- Oh, my. - I'm here to paint my car.

1773
01:06:15,121 --> 01:06:17,650
Once you customize the paint job, it becomes a one-of-a-kind car.

1774
01:06:17,651 --> 01:06:18,721
- Right. - Yes.

1775
01:06:18,891 --> 01:06:21,090
I'd get more attached to my car, and at competitions,

1776
01:06:21,091 --> 01:06:22,521
I can easily spot my car.

1777
01:06:25,261 --> 01:06:26,330
Let me hurry.

1778
01:06:26,331 --> 01:06:28,531
(He unpacks a mysterious box.)

1779
01:06:29,131 --> 01:06:31,130
I got this box from my legendary senior.

1780
01:06:31,131 --> 01:06:33,801
He used this box when he first got into model cars.

1781
01:06:34,171 --> 01:06:35,941
I have products for the paint job.

1782
01:06:36,771 --> 01:06:38,340
I can store three model cars.

1783
01:06:38,341 --> 01:06:40,640
He remodeled the box before giving it to me.

1784
01:06:40,641 --> 01:06:42,041
It's like a tool box.

1785
01:06:44,811 --> 01:06:47,581
I've been turning the motor whenever I had time.

1786
01:06:48,111 --> 01:06:49,451
I kept turning it on my way here.

1787
01:06:49,681 --> 01:06:51,221
- You did? - I did.

1788
01:06:53,051 --> 01:06:55,661
- You have to do that? - I need to break in the motor.

1789
01:06:55,991 --> 01:06:58,361
Let's say the motor is good for 80 years.

1790
01:06:58,531 --> 01:07:00,131
Then the car is the fastest at 79 years.

1791
01:07:00,291 --> 01:07:01,900
- It gets faster the more it's used? - Yes.

1792
01:07:01,901 --> 01:07:02,930
- The best scenario is... - Really?

1793
01:07:02,931 --> 01:07:04,207
That you use it for the competition...

1794
01:07:04,231 --> 01:07:05,830
- and it goes off right after. - And it's gone.

1795
01:07:05,831 --> 01:07:06,871
Right before it goes off.

1796
01:07:07,131 --> 01:07:09,141
- So you can beat me? - Of course.

1797
01:07:10,501 --> 01:07:13,811
I want to paint it green for the Christmas vibe.

1798
01:07:14,011 --> 01:07:16,181
I want to add red dots too.

1799
01:07:16,511 --> 01:07:18,910
- I want it to look like a tree. - I see. With red?

1800
01:07:18,911 --> 01:07:20,010
I'm curious.

1801
01:07:20,011 --> 01:07:23,751
I think I need to buy red and silver spray paint.

1802
01:07:24,081 --> 01:07:25,550
- First... - Good job.

1803
01:07:25,551 --> 01:07:28,020
Doing this toward the end of the year must be exciting.

1804
01:07:28,021 --> 01:07:29,060
Okay.

1805
01:07:29,061 --> 01:07:31,861
Then the silver spray...

1806
01:07:32,831 --> 01:07:35,091
(The colorful spray paint...)

1807
01:07:36,231 --> 01:07:37,330
(fills up the displays.)

1808
01:07:37,331 --> 01:07:38,431
My gosh. This is...

1809
01:07:38,701 --> 01:07:40,900
Wouldn't it cost a lot of money to buy the colors you want?

1810
01:07:40,901 --> 01:07:42,401
My gosh. Totally.

1811
01:07:43,141 --> 01:07:45,417
- Is there a pearly one? Yes. - You want glitters, right?

1812
01:07:45,441 --> 01:07:47,071
- It needs to glitter. - Let's see.

1813
01:07:47,441 --> 01:07:50,741
This one. You can pick 1 among these 3.

1814
01:07:51,541 --> 01:07:53,851
The colors come in different shades.

1815
01:07:53,981 --> 01:07:56,057
They're all silver, but one can be aluminium silver.

1816
01:07:56,081 --> 01:07:58,280
There are other shades of silver. So there's a big range.

1817
01:07:58,281 --> 01:07:59,991
- Like metallic silver. - That's right.

1818
01:08:00,191 --> 01:08:01,720
If you want a pearly one,

1819
01:08:01,721 --> 01:08:03,220
this one, My Car Silver, should be good.

1820
01:08:03,221 --> 01:08:04,721
This one? My Car Silver.

1821
01:08:05,191 --> 01:08:07,331
- You said you wanted red earlier. - Yes.

1822
01:08:07,531 --> 01:08:09,531
Then paint it gold first.

1823
01:08:09,831 --> 01:08:13,570
Then add a layer of clear red.

1824
01:08:13,571 --> 01:08:15,641
- The red shade will look vibrant. - I like that.

1825
01:08:15,971 --> 01:08:17,540
You can combine these two colors.

1826
01:08:17,541 --> 01:08:18,771
- These two. - I see.

1827
01:08:20,041 --> 01:08:22,141
- I like that. Let me try it. - Okay.

1828
01:08:23,081 --> 01:08:24,781
Hello. I'll buy them.

1829
01:08:25,511 --> 01:08:27,271
Would you like to collect membership points?

1830
01:08:27,681 --> 01:08:28,780
Yes.

1831
01:08:28,781 --> 01:08:30,280
Please check the last four digits.

1832
01:08:30,281 --> 01:08:31,720
(He frugally collects the points too.)

1833
01:08:31,721 --> 01:08:32,850
Thank you.

1834
01:08:32,851 --> 01:08:34,791
(He buys the spray paint.)

1835
01:08:35,151 --> 01:08:36,591
- I'll start with the spray. - Okay.

1836
01:08:38,461 --> 01:08:39,561
The paper...

1837
01:08:42,231 --> 01:08:43,361
(Attaching)

1838
01:08:44,401 --> 01:08:47,201
(He's attaching paper on the bottom of his model car?)

1839
01:08:49,541 --> 01:08:51,141
(Grabbing)

1840
01:08:52,011 --> 01:08:54,241
(He attaches a stick on the paper.)

1841
01:08:54,311 --> 01:08:55,740
- Okay. - For the airbrush.

1842
01:08:55,741 --> 01:08:56,941
(The mounting stick is ready.)

1843
01:08:57,041 --> 01:08:58,140
To dry it after applying the spray paint,

1844
01:08:58,141 --> 01:08:59,210
I need an elevated platform.

1845
01:08:59,211 --> 01:09:01,611
- I had to set that up too. - Right. You're a pro.

1846
01:09:02,081 --> 01:09:03,981
Spray both of them with silver.

1847
01:09:04,351 --> 01:09:05,451
Okay.

1848
01:09:06,121 --> 01:09:07,820
It's the back side of the store.

1849
01:09:07,821 --> 01:09:10,461
This is where people can paint their cars.

1850
01:09:12,431 --> 01:09:14,661
(Getting ready to paint it)

1851
01:09:15,261 --> 01:09:17,761
The first task is spraying the car.

1852
01:09:19,301 --> 01:09:21,831
(Applying a full coat of paint on the entire car)

1853
01:09:22,971 --> 01:09:25,771
(He gets started on painting the entire car.)

1854
01:09:27,811 --> 01:09:29,141
(Spraying)

1855
01:09:29,981 --> 01:09:32,151
(Checking the direction of the wind)

1856
01:09:32,811 --> 01:09:35,051
(He begins spraying paint.)

1857
01:09:36,121 --> 01:09:37,450
(After checking the paint, )

1858
01:09:37,451 --> 01:09:38,791
(he sprays some more.)

1859
01:09:39,951 --> 01:09:41,450
I need to add several layers.

1860
01:09:41,451 --> 01:09:42,931
Right. You need a lot of thin layers.

1861
01:09:45,661 --> 01:09:46,761
It's even.

1862
01:09:47,561 --> 01:09:49,760
I must check it after each spray.

1863
01:09:49,761 --> 01:09:51,431
That's how I need to layer the paint.

1864
01:09:51,831 --> 01:09:53,730
If I get greedy and keep spraying it nonstop,

1865
01:09:53,731 --> 01:09:54,871
it won't look good.

1866
01:09:55,871 --> 01:09:58,071
It's important for the coating to be even.

1867
01:09:59,711 --> 01:10:01,041
You look like a professional.

1868
01:10:04,941 --> 01:10:06,081
Bring it in.

1869
01:10:07,651 --> 01:10:08,781
You're done?

1870
01:10:12,021 --> 01:10:13,151
I must hurry.

1871
01:10:15,021 --> 01:10:18,730
(Whirring)

1872
01:10:18,731 --> 01:10:19,831
What are you doing?

1873
01:10:21,591 --> 01:10:23,151
You're not supposed to do it in winter.

1874
01:10:23,631 --> 01:10:25,801
You're supposed to do it in spring or summer.

1875
01:10:26,171 --> 01:10:27,970
But I couldn't wait and wanted to do it in winter.

1876
01:10:27,971 --> 01:10:29,171
So I used a special item.

1877
01:10:30,301 --> 01:10:31,401
My secret weapon.

1878
01:10:31,771 --> 01:10:33,811
- I can bring back summer with this. - Yes.

1879
01:10:34,311 --> 01:10:35,341
The hair dryer.

1880
01:10:35,581 --> 01:10:36,861
You're applying heat right away.

1881
01:10:38,411 --> 01:10:40,281
(Come on, dry.)

1882
01:10:41,081 --> 01:10:43,181
(Drying passionately)

1883
01:10:44,151 --> 01:10:45,451
(He sprays it outdoors.)

1884
01:10:47,151 --> 01:10:48,391
That's a lot of effort.

1885
01:10:48,591 --> 01:10:49,820
It takes a lot of effort.

1886
01:10:49,821 --> 01:10:51,061
(He dries it for a long while.)

1887
01:10:54,591 --> 01:10:55,631
You did a good job.

1888
01:10:56,801 --> 01:11:00,131
(Before the paint job, after the paint job)

1889
01:11:01,501 --> 01:11:03,641
(Grabbing the next item)

1890
01:11:07,311 --> 01:11:08,840
I'll cover this part.

1891
01:11:08,841 --> 01:11:09,880
(Putting a piece of tape on its body)

1892
01:11:09,881 --> 01:11:10,911
Then...

1893
01:11:11,511 --> 01:11:13,511
(Rubbing it, so there are no air bubbles)

1894
01:11:14,151 --> 01:11:16,321
I masked the car next.

1895
01:11:16,551 --> 01:11:18,680
I covered the parts of the car with masking tapes...

1896
01:11:18,681 --> 01:11:20,881
and used a knife to expose the parts I wanted to paint.

1897
01:11:20,951 --> 01:11:23,960
I sprayed the rest with green.

1898
01:11:23,961 --> 01:11:25,160
(Remove the tapes after spraying on it.)

1899
01:11:25,161 --> 01:11:26,560
You know what?

1900
01:11:26,561 --> 01:11:29,081
- That's the most important job. - That looks like a tough job.

1901
01:11:29,501 --> 01:11:30,631
Gosh, this isn't easy.

1902
01:11:32,401 --> 01:11:33,870
(Focusing all of his energy on his fingertips)

1903
01:11:33,871 --> 01:11:36,000
I bet you have to be super delicate.

1904
01:11:36,001 --> 01:11:37,841
(Focusing all of his energy on his fingertips)

1905
01:11:42,011 --> 01:11:44,340
I need to cut it with the knife without making any scratches.

1906
01:11:44,341 --> 01:11:46,251
- I must adjust my power well. - Right.

1907
01:11:49,321 --> 01:11:50,621
(Pulling)

1908
01:11:51,721 --> 01:11:53,550
- That's the hardest skill. - Of course.

1909
01:11:53,551 --> 01:11:54,750
(Scraping)

1910
01:11:54,751 --> 01:11:55,991
I'm making a scratch. Darn.

1911
01:11:56,361 --> 01:11:57,561
- Don't make a scratch. - No.

1912
01:11:58,361 --> 01:11:59,391
Oh, no.

1913
01:12:02,331 --> 01:12:05,400
(Screeching)

1914
01:12:05,401 --> 01:12:06,571
It's not coming out neatly.

1915
01:12:06,701 --> 01:12:07,970
What a mess.

1916
01:12:07,971 --> 01:12:08,971
(Upset)

1917
01:12:09,271 --> 01:12:12,070
(Sighing)

1918
01:12:12,071 --> 01:12:13,170
The scratches...

1919
01:12:13,171 --> 01:12:14,171
(Clicking his tongue)

1920
01:12:17,281 --> 01:12:20,251
(However, he doesn't give up and focuses on it again.)

1921
01:12:23,521 --> 01:12:24,550
(He manages to remove the tape without any scratches this time.)

1922
01:12:24,551 --> 01:12:25,621
I got it.

1923
01:12:26,891 --> 01:12:28,921
(Careful)

1924
01:12:30,121 --> 01:12:32,231
(Is this good now?)

1925
01:12:33,261 --> 01:12:34,360
Look. Does it look good?

1926
01:12:34,361 --> 01:12:35,431
Yes, it looks neat.

1927
01:12:36,831 --> 01:12:39,371
(He sprays the car again.)

1928
01:12:40,301 --> 01:12:41,901
It's my favorite color.

1929
01:12:41,971 --> 01:12:43,040
The dinosaur color.

1930
01:12:43,041 --> 01:12:44,921
(It's getting painted with his favorite color.)

1931
01:12:46,011 --> 01:12:48,371
The more layers it gets, the prettier it looks.

1932
01:12:48,811 --> 01:12:50,211
It's rewarding and fun.

1933
01:12:50,781 --> 01:12:52,551
(On an infinite loop)

1934
01:12:53,951 --> 01:12:56,281
(I just need to wrap it up nicely.)

1935
01:13:00,391 --> 01:13:02,360
(Satisfied with the paint job)

1936
01:13:02,361 --> 01:13:04,021
I'm curious about the finished look.

1937
01:13:05,961 --> 01:13:09,031
(Let me see.)

1938
01:13:11,531 --> 01:13:13,031
It's fun to remove the tapes.

1939
01:13:13,171 --> 01:13:15,301
- That was a nerve-racking moment. - Right.

1940
01:13:19,671 --> 01:13:22,110
- I see. The silver parts remain. - Yes.

1941
01:13:22,111 --> 01:13:23,871
(The masked parts retain the silver finish.)

1942
01:13:24,811 --> 01:13:26,751
- My gosh. - It came out nicely.

1943
01:13:27,151 --> 01:13:29,581
Okay.

1944
01:13:29,881 --> 01:13:31,451
That must feel good.

1945
01:13:32,081 --> 01:13:33,491
- Okay. - That's amazing.

1946
01:13:34,291 --> 01:13:36,390
This looks pretty good. It should do it.

1947
01:13:36,391 --> 01:13:37,621
(Looking clean)

1948
01:13:38,621 --> 01:13:39,631
What?

1949
01:13:40,831 --> 01:13:44,461
I set the overall color in the first step.

1950
01:13:44,561 --> 01:13:47,470
Next, I mixed the paint with the paint thinner.

1951
01:13:47,471 --> 01:13:49,701
I can adjust the thickness of the paint with it.

1952
01:13:50,101 --> 01:13:51,601
(Dabbing the paint)

1953
01:13:53,671 --> 01:13:56,011
(Brushing the paint to create a one-of-a-kind car)

1954
01:13:57,541 --> 01:13:59,551
- Did you get some stuff done? - You're here.

1955
01:14:00,700 --> 01:14:02,140
(Putting it down)

1956
01:14:02,640 --> 01:14:03,899
You already painted it yesterday, right?

1957
01:14:03,900 --> 01:14:05,409
Of course. Wait.

1958
01:14:05,410 --> 01:14:06,769
Let me see.

1959
01:14:06,770 --> 01:14:08,169
- Is he your hobby friend? - Let's see.

1960
01:14:08,170 --> 01:14:09,339
- He's my neighborhood friend. - How did it come out?

1961
01:14:09,340 --> 01:14:11,340
He and I got into model cars together.

1962
01:14:12,980 --> 01:14:14,260
I bet you want to beat me today.

1963
01:14:15,450 --> 01:14:18,120
- I kept running my motor yesterday. - Okay.

1964
01:14:18,220 --> 01:14:20,119
I see. Do you think it got faster?

1965
01:14:20,120 --> 01:14:21,550
I won't go easy on you today.

1966
01:14:22,020 --> 01:14:23,119
(Inhaling sharply)

1967
01:14:23,120 --> 01:14:24,420
All right.

1968
01:14:25,020 --> 01:14:27,060
(Whirring)

1969
01:14:28,060 --> 01:14:30,800
From the sound of the motor, you can never beat me.

1970
01:14:31,060 --> 01:14:32,260
That's a total act of bravado.

1971
01:14:32,400 --> 01:14:33,770
I can tell just by the sound.

1972
01:14:37,800 --> 01:14:39,040
What? Polka dots?

1973
01:14:41,340 --> 01:14:43,840
What kind of pattern is that?

1974
01:14:44,810 --> 01:14:46,110
The theme is the Christmas tree.

1975
01:14:46,810 --> 01:14:48,879
- On the Christmas tree... - So they're the ornaments.

1976
01:14:48,880 --> 01:14:51,080
(Adding the gold ornaments to the green Christmas tree)

1977
01:14:51,780 --> 01:14:53,220
(Shy)

1978
01:14:55,390 --> 01:14:56,760
(Poking)

1979
01:14:57,820 --> 01:15:00,389
(Chan Bin adds black dots to the red car.)

1980
01:15:00,390 --> 01:15:01,590
Is it a watermelon theme?

1981
01:15:02,330 --> 01:15:03,860
I want mine to give a Ferrari vibe.

1982
01:15:04,060 --> 01:15:05,259
It looks nice.

1983
01:15:05,260 --> 01:15:06,830
- Oh, yes. - What?

1984
01:15:08,100 --> 01:15:09,440
(Putting it on)

1985
01:15:10,570 --> 01:15:11,599
(What do you think?)

1986
01:15:11,600 --> 01:15:13,400
- Does it look good? - It looks amazing. Hey.

1987
01:15:13,840 --> 01:15:16,840
Actually, I quite like mine. Look.

1988
01:15:17,710 --> 01:15:20,449
(Trailing off)

1989
01:15:20,450 --> 01:15:21,510
Yes.

1990
01:15:22,550 --> 01:15:24,079
It looks better in person.

1991
01:15:24,080 --> 01:15:25,750
They should give compliments.

1992
01:15:25,950 --> 01:15:28,126
- They're just watching. - I already feel so close to them.

1993
01:15:28,150 --> 01:15:30,120
- Right. So... - You guys bonded a lot today.

1994
01:15:30,590 --> 01:15:32,130
Well, it looked really good.

1995
01:15:32,960 --> 01:15:34,660
The picture on the left looks great.

1996
01:15:37,030 --> 01:15:38,770
(Ju Seung's and Chan Bin's model cars)

1997
01:15:39,630 --> 01:15:40,799
Doesn't it look cool?

1998
01:15:40,800 --> 01:15:42,440
Ju Seung's car looks better.

1999
01:15:43,140 --> 01:15:44,270
I like his friend's.

2000
01:15:45,510 --> 01:15:47,140
(They're ready to race.)

2001
01:15:49,580 --> 01:15:51,239
I should time them.

2002
01:15:51,240 --> 01:15:52,549
- Let's do that. - Yes.

2003
01:15:52,550 --> 01:15:54,510
(They try a test run first.)

2004
01:15:55,010 --> 01:15:57,550
All right. Turn on the app.

2005
01:15:58,380 --> 01:15:59,650
There's an app for it?

2006
01:15:59,750 --> 01:16:01,696
- The records are precise with it. - I see. One at a time?

2007
01:16:01,720 --> 01:16:03,290
- When it passes through? - Yes.

2008
01:16:03,460 --> 01:16:05,459
It records the start and finish times.

2009
01:16:05,460 --> 01:16:07,140
(The app records lap times automatically.)

2010
01:16:07,460 --> 01:16:08,560
Here it goes.

2011
01:16:09,300 --> 01:16:10,760
(With the tuning complete, )

2012
01:16:12,030 --> 01:16:14,100
(it's time to race!)

2013
01:16:14,500 --> 01:16:15,570
Here it goes.

2014
01:16:16,040 --> 01:16:17,069
(Whirring)

2015
01:16:17,070 --> 01:16:18,500
Should I put it on Track One?

2016
01:16:18,740 --> 01:16:20,070
(All right.)

2017
01:16:25,810 --> 01:16:27,110
(Rattling)

2018
01:16:27,580 --> 01:16:28,650
It almost jumped out.

2019
01:16:29,180 --> 01:16:30,719
Let's go!

2020
01:16:30,720 --> 01:16:32,080
(Dangerously staying on the track)

2021
01:16:32,820 --> 01:16:33,849
(It quickly speeds through the curves.)

2022
01:16:33,850 --> 01:16:35,290
I see. That's how it goes.

2023
01:16:36,160 --> 01:16:37,189
(Swooshing)

2024
01:16:37,190 --> 01:16:39,489
- Gosh, it almost flew. - It's so fast.

2025
01:16:39,490 --> 01:16:40,959
Great.

2026
01:16:40,960 --> 01:16:42,499
- Great. - When I was here last time,

2027
01:16:42,500 --> 01:16:44,030
my record was 19 seconds.

2028
01:16:44,700 --> 01:16:45,769
(Ju Seung's best record is 19 seconds.)

2029
01:16:45,770 --> 01:16:47,170
That's super fast.

2030
01:16:49,370 --> 01:16:51,300
- What's the record? - How many seconds?

2031
01:16:52,140 --> 01:16:54,539
Twenty-two seconds.

2032
01:16:54,540 --> 01:16:55,860
(His time gets 3 seconds slower.)

2033
01:16:56,080 --> 01:16:57,180
What's wrong with this?

2034
01:16:58,340 --> 01:17:00,810
- He's disappointed. - Gosh, it's 22 seconds.

2035
01:17:01,050 --> 01:17:03,079
Isn't that pretty fast?

2036
01:17:03,080 --> 01:17:05,520
It is. But my previous record was in the 19-second range.

2037
01:17:05,990 --> 01:17:08,590
Here's what you must know. It takes three seconds...

2038
01:17:08,990 --> 01:17:10,090
to finish half a lap.

2039
01:17:11,720 --> 01:17:12,840
I know what I'm going to do.

2040
01:17:15,530 --> 01:17:17,060
I'll clean the motor.

2041
01:17:21,930 --> 01:17:23,740
Gosh, how fast do you want it to be?

2042
01:17:24,500 --> 01:17:25,969
(Inspecting the equipment to set a new record)

2043
01:17:25,970 --> 01:17:27,370
In my opinion,

2044
01:17:28,510 --> 01:17:31,580
it could have been the condition of the motor.

2045
01:17:31,780 --> 01:17:33,749
The rechargeable battery has to be full too.

2046
01:17:33,750 --> 01:17:35,720
And I must insert it right before the race...

2047
01:17:35,780 --> 01:17:36,949
and when it's warm.

2048
01:17:36,950 --> 01:17:38,620
- Really? - Timing is important too.

2049
01:17:38,720 --> 01:17:40,190
It's like that movie, "F1."

2050
01:17:40,520 --> 01:17:42,890
A group of people switches parts in the middle of the race.

2051
01:17:43,120 --> 01:17:45,659
They work on the car like filling up the gas and so on.

2052
01:17:45,660 --> 01:17:46,690
It's the same thing.

2053
01:17:49,500 --> 01:17:50,799
(Replacing the parts in a matter of seconds)

2054
01:17:50,800 --> 01:17:52,720
- They must do it quickly. My gosh. - That's it.

2055
01:17:53,530 --> 01:17:55,299
- It's just like the movie, "F1." - It is.

2056
01:17:55,300 --> 01:17:56,300
(It's like a scene from the movie, "F1.")

2057
01:17:56,301 --> 01:17:58,400
I should cover up the brake.

2058
01:17:58,700 --> 01:18:00,269
When I cover up the brake with a sticker,

2059
01:18:00,270 --> 01:18:02,810
it gets slipperier. So it can go faster.

2060
01:18:02,910 --> 01:18:04,009
- I see. - When it jumps...

2061
01:18:04,010 --> 01:18:05,570
- You reduce the friction. - That's it.

2062
01:18:05,610 --> 01:18:06,649
But it gets disqualified...

2063
01:18:06,650 --> 01:18:07,679
- if it goes out of the track. - It must stay within the track.

2064
01:18:07,680 --> 01:18:10,279
There are only two factors. Safety and speed.

2065
